WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.080
SCP-999, also known as The Tickle Monster.

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.120
It’s one of the most adorable, beloved,
and undeniably wholesome anomalies ever to

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.249
exist in the SCP Foundation’s containment
facilities.

00:00:13.249 --> 00:00:19.410
Its mere presence can cause joy and comfort,
cure depression and other mental illnesses,

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:24.320
and even sometimes cause violent and unpredictable
creatures to really mellow out.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.640
If you’re a fan of this channel, chances
are that you’re a big fan of SCP-999, too.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:34.579
But that doesn’t mean everyone is on board:
As we all know, there are plenty of entities

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:39.460
and groups in the SCP Universe that are downright
evil, and as a result, would love to see this

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.289
little blob of pure joy crushed to a pulp
or sacrificed to a cosmic horror.

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:46.809
But you can’t ever underestimate -
wait a second.

00:00:46.809 --> 00:00:48.530
Is that the Containment Breach alarm?

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:51.390
All Foundation staff members report to the
affected cell immediately!

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:56.819
It looks like an SCP has escaped containment
and is now… in our world?

00:00:56.819 --> 00:01:02.589
That’s right, SCP-999 has broken out of
SCP Foundation control and now you can finally

00:01:02.589 --> 00:01:05.250
have a Tickle Monster of your very own!

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:06.250
In plush form!

00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:10.659
This super adorable plush from SCP Swag is
11 inches of huggable, squeezable, joy and

00:01:10.659 --> 00:01:14.950
now that the Tickle Monster is out of containment,
you can bring it into your own home.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.909
Tickle Monster Plushes are available for pre-order
now, and all orders made in the next ten days

00:01:18.909 --> 00:01:21.729
also get a special limited First Edition Card!

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:26.259
Worldwide shipping is available, so go to
SCP Swag dot com right now and pre order your

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:27.670
own Tickle Monster!

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:32.219
And let us know in the comments what SCP anomalies
you want to see in plush form next!

00:01:32.219 --> 00:01:39.500
But as we were saying - you can’t ever underestimate
SCP-999: Not only has it tickled SCP-682 into

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.750
submission, there are also certain theories
floating around the foundation that it will

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.979
one day grow so powerful, its forces of pure
goodness and joy can overthrow the Scarlet

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:50.289
King himself.

00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:55.480
That’s why today we’re throwing the Tickle
Monster into a kind of Royal Rumble with all

00:01:55.480 --> 00:02:00.100
the baddest dudes the Foundation has ever
encountered, and we’re going to give our

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:06.240
theories on how SCP-999 might somehow find
the good in even the blackest of hearts.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:13.120
First, SCP-096 - The Shy Guy, a killing machine
so brutal, direct, and opaque in its motives

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.710
that some have even questioned whether it
actually has sentience.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:20.530
However, we’d personally stake our claim
that it does.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:26.200
When a photo of this savage beast was taken
with SCP-978, the Desire Camera - a camera

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:31.230
that shows the deepest desires of its subjects
- it revealed that the Shy Guy secretly just

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.650
had the desire to disappear.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:38.170
Not only does this suggest that the monster
may not actually like killing people, but

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:43.470
the very idea that it can have a desire also
implies some level of intelligence.

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.650
But how would SCP-999 enter the mix?

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:50.240
Well, we know that 096 is an anxious creature.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:55.129
It spends the majority of its time just pacing
its cell, and when someone sees its face,

00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:59.340
it begins sobbing uncontrollably before entering
its rage state.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.879
Does this sound like a happy entity to you?

00:03:01.879 --> 00:03:06.500
If the Shy Guy encountered 999 at its full
joy-giving power, we personally think that

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.900
it might finally chill out a little.

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:12.849
Perhaps it’d take a moment to breathe and
contemplate life a little more.

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:17.450
Maybe it’d wonder why it’s so ashamed
of its face, and feels the need to hunt down

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.709
and kill anyone who sees it.

00:03:19.709 --> 00:03:22.040
After all, there are much uglier anomalies.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.040
Like SCP-106!

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.879
He’s the next monster to join this weird,
wild cage match against SCP-999.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:36.800
While 096 is violent, 106 is downright malevolent
- he’s not just sentient, but extremely

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.159
intelligent.

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:42.860
The Old Man loves causing pain and suffering
for his own perverse pleasure, just as much

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:45.959
as heavy-hitters like 682.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:49.360
So surely 999 would have its work cut out
for it here?

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.599
Well, not necessarily.

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:55.410
There are two leading theories about who 106
actually is.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:59.329
One being the Scranton theory and the other,
the Corporal Lawrence theory.

00:03:59.329 --> 00:04:04.939
The first dictates that 106 is the result
of Dr. Robert Scranton, physically and mentally

00:04:04.939 --> 00:04:10.909
transformed by his time in SCP-3001, the terrifying
Red Reality.

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:15.599
The second theory was that he was a World
War One soldier known as Corporal Lawrence,

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:20.570
whose anomalous encounter in the trenches
turned him into the beast he is today.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:26.199
In either case, he’s a man shaped by pain
and anomalous trauma - much like 096, the

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:31.699
Desire Camera revealed an insight into 106’s
mind: His greatest desire consists of him

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:37.380
walking across a field towards an old house,
where an old woman smiles and waits for him.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:41.039
Many believe this old woman to be his estranged
wife.

00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:47.080
Perhaps an encounter with SCP-999 would cause
106’s sadism to abate, reminding him of

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.539
the humanity he once had.

00:04:49.539 --> 00:04:54.460
Maybe he’d become a kindly old man in the
aftermath - who prefers Werther’s Originals

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:59.720
to violence and spinning long, rambling yarns
about the war rather than chasing people around

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.819
his terrifying pocket dimension.

00:05:01.819 --> 00:05:05.830
It’s a thought so sweet it could almost
make you sick.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.580
Thankfully, one of our favorite doctors is
next on the list - specifically, the Plague

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.900
Doctor, SCP-049.

00:05:13.900 --> 00:05:18.949
While he definitely isn’t as dangerous or
malicious as either of his predecessors, 049

00:05:18.949 --> 00:05:22.580
has racked up quite a body count in his hundreds
of years of operations.

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:29.449
He sees Pestilence everywhere he goes, except
within, and can kill with a mere touch.

00:05:29.449 --> 00:05:35.319
However, his deadly touch only seems to apply
to non-anomalous animals and humans, not other

00:05:35.319 --> 00:05:41.111
anomalies, so he definitely couldn’t harm
999, and The Tickle Monster, conversely, could

00:05:41.111 --> 00:05:42.750
definitely touch him back.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.690
While the Plague Doctor is the serious type,
he might not be able to keep his bedside manner

00:05:47.690 --> 00:05:49.580
after a serious tickling.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:54.009
And we’d be more than willing to hedge our
bets on him having the laugh of an angel.

00:05:54.009 --> 00:06:00.020
While 049 may have folded in the face of 999’s
tickling wrath, our next contestant is as

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.510
solid as a rock.

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:04.210
Well, technically as solid as concrete.

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:10.100
That’s because it’s SCP-173, also known
as the Sculpture or The Peanut.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:15.130
It shows no emotions, and murders anything
that blinks in its presence by snapping its

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.130
neck.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:21.190
But 999 doesn’t even have bones, let alone
a neck, so SCP-173 has nothing with which

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:23.509
to threaten this happy little blob.

00:06:23.509 --> 00:06:26.550
And what about SCP-999’s counter-offensive?

00:06:26.550 --> 00:06:32.260
If the Tickle Monster got its slime all over
SCP-173, it might finally reform this statuesque

00:06:32.260 --> 00:06:35.030
serial killer through prolonged exposure.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:40.520
Maybe after that 173 will give relaxing neck
massages rather than snapping them.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:45.139
But while the Sculpture may be intimidating,
it’s nothing compared to an unkillable,

00:06:45.139 --> 00:06:47.260
mass-murdering blademaster, right?

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:52.640
Of course, we’re talking about SCP-076,
also known as Able.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:58.180
No matter how many times he gets put down,
he keeps coming back, with unparalleled skills

00:06:58.180 --> 00:07:02.580
in physical combat and the ability to pull
huge blades out of thin air.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.639
He also appears to be fueled by pure, unstoppable
rage.

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:11.310
So how on earth could our adorable tickle
monster possibly go toe to toe with a swordsman

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:15.919
who cuts through elite Mobile Task Force soldiers
like a hot knife through a D-Class?

00:07:15.919 --> 00:07:21.910
Much like SCP-106, it seems like a lot of
Able’s rage is rooted in a deep pain caused

00:07:21.910 --> 00:07:23.370
by his past.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:28.310
If he truly is the biblical Abel, it’s likely
that his rage stems from being the very first

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:35.250
murder victim, betrayed and killed by his
brother, Cain - now known as SCP-073.

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:40.539
Spending time with SCP-999 might finally calm
him down enough to actually work through some

00:07:40.539 --> 00:07:43.539
of these issues and come to a sense of closure.

00:07:43.539 --> 00:07:48.940
Maybe, with SCP-999 at his side, Able could
attend some therapy sessions with Foundation

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:54.590
psychologists until he finally felt as though
he’d moved past his murderous urges - perhaps

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:57.289
even working up to family counseling with
Cain.

00:07:57.289 --> 00:08:01.599
He could then re-enter society, and reapply
his expert knife skills and become a Bobby

00:08:01.599 --> 00:08:07.120
Flay-style celebrity chef - except one who
could actually flay you if you got on his

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.120
bad side.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.180
But let’s talk about an SCP that’s frankly
dangerous to even discuss.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.789
I am of course referring to SCP-2521.

00:08:15.789 --> 00:08:19.240
Oh great, I’m not dead.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.240
Wonderful.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:21.970
Let’s carry on.

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:26.620
2521 is attracted to any information about
it, written or spoken.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:31.789
It will immediately appear upon the creation
of this information and steal either the information

00:08:31.789 --> 00:08:36.370
itself or the person disseminating it in the
case of verbal words.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:43.610
If someone were to pass SCP-999 a fact sheet
on SCP-2521, it would inevitably manifest

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.590
and prepare to throw down.

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:52.270
But perhaps the positive influence of SCP-999
would change SCP-2521’s tune.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:56.560
Rather than obsessively stealing information
about itself, the being may instead finally

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.150
open up and speak about itself.

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:03.190
We might even learn some interesting things,
like the fact that it used to have a bowling

00:09:03.190 --> 00:09:06.270
team with SCP-106 and SCP-049.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:13.460
He also loves knitting-
Oh, come on, not again!

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:21.490
Now, how about we go for something a little
closer to human: SCP-082, Fernand the Cannibal,

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:27.060
a huge, ogre-like humanoid that has a penchant
for pathological lies and also devouring human

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:28.400
heads.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:34.660
And, well, the rest of the body too, if he’s
worked up enough of an appetite.

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:39.810
He’s super strong and has a hide so thick
that seemingly no weapon can penetrate it.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:44.390
How could SCP-999 possibly go a round with
a behemoth like this?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.400
Lucky for 999, Fernand has an extremely cheerful
temperament.

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:52.640
If a potential victim can keep him amused,
often listening and playing along with his

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:57.350
elaborate fantasies, it massively increases
their chance of survival.

00:09:57.350 --> 00:10:02.730
And considering SCP-999 is literally a good
vibes machine, there’s a good chance that

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:07.190
it’d keep Fernand so amused that the thought
of getting hangry wouldn’t even cross his

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.190
mind.

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:12.010
Once again, little SCP-999 takes home the
W.

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.100
But what about a real sadist?

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:19.880
A truly heartless monster whose commitment
to focused, endless cruelty is genuinely unparalleled?

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:24.170
We’re talking about the being from SCP-3999.

00:10:24.170 --> 00:10:28.830
This terrifyingly powerful reality warper
hasn’t racked up scores of victims, because

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:31.970
it prefers the quality of suffering over quantity.

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:36.980
It’ll select a single victim, trap them
in their own personal hell, and spend a literal

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:42.040
eternity conceiving every possible torture
and torment to break the spirit and body of

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.250
the victim, never giving them the luxury of
death.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:50.680
However, if any entity could turn the tables
and break the spirit of SCP-3999, it would

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:53.290
be SCP-999.

00:10:53.290 --> 00:10:57.600
Picture it: Thousands of years where the monster
tries everything it can to break the Tickle

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:03.810
Monster’s spirit, only to find its own spirit
being broken as 999 doesn’t succumb to any

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:07.930
of it and continues to project love and kindness
throughout.

00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:11.220
Could you imagine anything more frustrating
for a creature like 3999?

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:16.320
Eventually, it would probably get so frustrated
that it would let 999 go, and go find some

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:19.620
hapless Foundation researcher to torture instead.

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:24.521
Going up against a single anomalous being,
regardless of its power, is one thing, but

00:11:24.521 --> 00:11:28.400
taking on an entire group is another challenge
for SCP-999.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:35.800
What if 999 became trapped in SCP-3008, the
endless Ikea, surrounded by the deadly Staff

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:37.430
in the middle of the night?

00:11:37.430 --> 00:11:42.360
Our theory is that the positive presence of
SCP-999 would really help the nightmarish,

00:11:42.360 --> 00:11:47.170
malformed Staff of this accursed Ikea, turn
their lives around and start creating a more

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.180
positive work environment around the store.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:53.490
Rather than trying to chase the survivors
trapped inside the store and beat them to

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:58.010
death, they would instead help them find the
ideal furniture for enhancing their lifestyle

00:11:58.010 --> 00:12:00.840
if ever they managed to escape the building.

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:04.960
999 would help them go from horrifying to
helpful in no time.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:08.660
It’d be so nice in there that the survivors
wouldn’t even want to leave!

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.380
But what about groups of interest?

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:14.520
Let’s say the Chaos Insurgency has broken
into a containment site in another one of

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.880
its classic raids against the Foundation.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:21.350
Would a group of elite Chaos Insurgency operatives
be able to take down the Tickle Monster?

00:12:21.350 --> 00:12:22.350
We think not.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:26.920
While these anomaly-stealing militants may
be hardcore compared to your average joe,

00:12:26.920 --> 00:12:33.490
they’re nowhere near as hateful or irredeemable
as the likes of 682 or 106.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:38.080
Chances are if they spent any amount of time
around 999, they’d experience a sudden sense

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:42.450
of mellowness, and begin to rethink all of
their poor life choices.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:44.100
But what about the GOC?

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:48.730
Those government stooges obsessed with killing
any anomaly they can get their hands on?

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:54.010
Personally, we theorize that a run-in with
SCP-999, and the immensely positive feelings

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:58.560
it causes, would cause them to reevaluate
their entire philosophy on the anomalies they

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:04.150
encounter and lead them to restructure their
entire organization from the ground up.

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:09.360
Perhaps they’d even promote SCP-999 to the
position of Undersecretary-General, and perhaps

00:13:09.360 --> 00:13:13.650
even change the meaning of the group’s acronym
to “Givers of Cuddles” in honor of their

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:15.740
new leader and direction.

00:13:15.740 --> 00:13:16.740
We can dream, right?

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:22.590
But let’s end this dream with a nightmare:
The Scarlet King, the most dangerous being

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:29.420
in the entire multiverse, who is also strongly
believed to be SCP-999’s real father.

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.460
Awkward.

00:13:30.460 --> 00:13:33.380
Can ultimate good someday defeat ultimate
evil?

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:37.900
According to ancient Daevite prophecies - a
terrifying historical culture that worshipped

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:44.140
the Scarlet King - yes, it can, if given the
time and nurturing it needs to reach full

00:13:44.140 --> 00:13:45.140
power.

00:13:45.140 --> 00:13:46.900
How exactly would that battle play out?

00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:51.570
Well...it’s difficult to even theorize,
but chances are, it’d be a battle of truly

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:53.450
biblical proportions.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:57.330
And if ever the Scarlet King did breach our
dimension, it’s safe to say that you’d

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:01.020
want your own little SCP-999 close at hand.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.560
And now you can!

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:06.590
Go to SCP Swag dot come and pre-order a Tickle
Monster plush of your very own!

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:10.710
It doesn’t even need any anomalous powers
to bring you a ridiculous amount of joy.

00:14:10.710 --> 00:14:15.310
Orders placed in the next ten days get a special
